      <h2>What the SORP 2026 asks</h2>
      <p>It applies to reporting periods beginning on or after 1 January 2026.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tier 1 (income up to £500,000):</strong> summarise main achievements and consider the difference made to beneficiaries and society.</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 2 and 3 (over £500,000):</strong> explain the impact the charity is making and consider the long-term effect of its work.</li>
        <li>The report should link to the financial statements and say honestly what can and cannot yet be shown.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Why it is hard</h2>
      <p>Most charities know they make a difference. Fewer can show it in a form trustees can sign off. We act as a critical friend, so the report says what the evidence supports and nothing more.</p>
    </div>
